Forward claude.* WebSocket methods to the phone/Mac connector.

nocturned only routes an explicit allow-list of methods to the connector; its
default arm answers "Unknown method" to the UI. Claude Mode needs the device to
call claude.* on the Mac daemon (via the Nocturne connector's relay), so add one
match-guard arm ahead of the default. Events flowing the other way (phone → UI)
already pass through verbatim and need no change.

scripts/build-nocturned.sh applies this and cross-compiles the result in Docker
in about 90 seconds; the notes below are for doing it by hand.

Apply in a checkout of https://github.com/usenocturne/nocturned:

    cd /path/to/nocturned
    git apply /path/to/claude-thing/patches/nocturned-claude-forward.patch

--- a/src/app/websocket_handler.rs
+++ b/src/app/websocket_handler.rs
@@
                 "audio.record.start" => {
+                    // (unchanged — anchor for context)
                 }
@@
-                _ => {
+                m if m.starts_with("claude.") => {
+                    let claude_request = serde_json::json!({
+                        "method": method,
+                        "params": data.get("params").unwrap_or(&serde_json::Value::Null)
+                    });
+
+                    info!("Routing WebSocket Claude request to connector: {}", method);
+
+                    return Ok(Some(AppMessage {
+                        id: message.id,
+                        protocol: "com.usenocturne.daemon".to_string(),
+                        session_id: message.session_id,
+                        data: Bytes::from(serde_json::to_vec(&claude_request)?),
+                    }));
+                }
+                _ => {
                     warn!("Unknown WebSocket method: {}", method);

NOTE: this file documents the edit rather than being a byte-exact diff — line
numbers in websocket_handler.rs shift between nocturne releases. The edit is a
single new match arm inserted immediately before the `_ =>` arm (~line 286 in
the v4.0.7 tree), cloned from the phone-forwarding body used by the spotify.*
allow-list arm (~line 169). Nothing else changes.

After building, either flash the new firmware normally or inject just the
rebuilt nocturned binary into an existing zip with
`node scripts/inject-firmware.js --nocturned <path-to-binary>`.
